      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "1 mL of 10^-2 M neodymium nitrate in 0.01 M HNO3 was evaporated to dryness at about 100–120 °C. The residue was dissolved in a minimum quantity of water and 0.3 mL of 0.1 M citric acid aqueous solution was added. After complete dissolution, 1 M KOH was added dropwise to pH about 7–9. An equimolar quantity of 0.1 M [Co(NH3)6]Cl3 solution was finally added. After a few hours of storage at 6–10 °C, crystals formed. Crystals were filtered off, washed with cold water, and dried at ambient temperature.",
